<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese January car sales down 7.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Portuguese January car sales down 7.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese Auto-Dealers Association (ACAP) announced the following new car registrations:</p>
<p>January 1997	    15,970 vs 17,231 (minus 7.3 pct)</p>
<p>	 January by manufacturers market share</p>
<p>(percentage in brackets), comparative figures</p>
<p>			 refer to same period 1996:</p>
<p>    Fiat	 2,268 (14.20) vs 2,276 (13.21)</p>
<p>    Renault    2,030 (12.71) vs 2,207 (12.81)</p>
<p>    Opel	 1,993 (12.48) vs 2,150 (12.48)</p>
<p>    Volkswagen 1,391 (08.71) vs 1,484 (08.61)</p>
<p>    Ford	 1,277 (08.00) vs 1,901 (11.03)</p>
<p>    Citroen    1,180 (07.39) vs 1,020 (05.92)</p>
<p>    Peugeot    1,020 (06.39) vs 1,292 (07.50)</p>
<p>    Honda	  703 (04.40) vs   770 (04.47)</p>
<p>    Mitsubishi   466 (02.92) vs   229 (01.33)</p>
<p>    Audi	   465 (02.91) vs   223 (01.29)</p>
</text>
